    overview: "Design with Blocks (kayashaolu/systemthinkinglab) turns architecture-level product design into a Claude Code plugin. You describe the product; the skill decomposes features into Service, Worker, Key-Value Store, File Store, Queue, Relational Database, and Vector Database (plus User / External Service / Time), then produces a buildable design document with per-block technology recommendations.\n\nMagier lists it as essential for product/UX designers who need structure before visual polish—pairing with Review with Blocks for critique. It is process/architecture design, not a visual theme skill.",
